-# ScriptRunner Workflows and Transition Interceptors
+# Scripted Workflows and Transition Helpers
 
 ## Overview
 
 In traditional project management tools, workflow rules are either simple notification triggers or inflexible webhooks that fire only *after* a change has occurred. If an issue is improperly moved to "Done" without meeting code coverage requirements or QA verification, the damage is already done.
 
-👍kanban implements a **ScriptRunner-Style Workflow Engine** with **Pre-Transition Interceptors**. When an operator or agent attempts to move a work item between states (`from_state -> to_state`), the transition is intercepted and evaluated through an ordered pipeline of synchronous validators, field mutators, and asynchronous AI agent gates.
+👍kanban implements a **Scripted Workflow Engine** with **Pre-Transition Helpers**. When an operator or agent attempts to move a work item between states (`from_state -> to_state`), the transition is evaluated through an ordered pipeline of synchronous validators, field mutators, and asynchronous AI agent gates.
 
